# Outgrowing-Ag: Landowner Partnership Script & Talking Points

## Objective
To secure initial land shares/leases from local property owners and agricultural producers by positioning Outgrowing-Ag as a professional, zero-burden solution to regional labor shortages, while introducing our supervised dual-track workforce model.

---

## 1. The Opening Hook (Establishing Common Ground)
"Hello [Name], I’m reaching out on behalf of Outgrowing-Ag. We know firsthand how fierce the agricultural labor shortages are right now across the Willamette Valley, and many property owners are sitting on valuable acreage that’s tough to keep managed. 

We provide a structured, supervised workforce solution designed to take the heavy lifting completely off your plate while bringing idle land into productive use."

## 2. The Core Value Proposition (The "Zero-Burden" Pitch)
* **What we do:** "We bring an experienced core team that handles initial site setup, infrastructure management, planting, and harvest execution."
* **How we protect your time:** "You aren't managing extra labor or fielding day-to-day issues. Our team operates under a strict professional project-management framework—we handle the logistics, and you get your crops in the ground and harvested on time."

## 3. Addressing Key Concerns (Proactive Reassurance)
* **On Liability & Control:** 
  > "Everything we do is governed by clear written agreements, defined site boundaries, and strict safety protocols. Our workers operate under direct supervision at all times."
* **On Tax Deferrals (EFU / Farm-Forest Land):** 
  > "Our agricultural and soil health tracks actively support active land management, helping ensure your property maintains its intended agricultural utility and compliance."
* **On Crop Timing & Overwintering:** 
  > "We build our planting and harvest schedules with seasonal transitions in mind—including cover crops and overwintering strategies—ensuring the land is properly cared for year-round."

## 4. The Broader Mission (Community Impact)
"Beyond solving immediate labor and harvest needs, our crews are part of a structured program that provides dignified employment pathways, skills training, and stipends for individuals—including veterans and underemployed community members—rebuilding their workforce footing."

## 5. The Closing Call to Action
"We’d love to walk the property with you, look at a small test plot or designated acreage, and see how a partnership could benefit both your land and our community mission. Are you available for a quick site visit sometime next week?"
